        "title": "A blast from the past, with some tips for the future",
        "body": [
          {
            "text": "The art in this book will take you back to your childhood. And the words within it will hopefully help refine you as an adult by teaching kindness-driven approaches that create happiness for yourself and those around you."
          }
        ],
        "image": {
          "role": "case.screenshot",
          "src": "/images/1675121290-main_book_cover.jpg"
        },
        "highlight": "blast",
        "cta": {
          "label": "Get the book!",
          "href": "https://www.findworkhappiness.com"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "image-fade-in",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "instant-visible"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "content.title-text",
      "content": {
        "title": "Changing the norm really is possible",
        "body": [
          {
            "text": "It's a leader's job to set those around them up for success. To start doing that, you first have to get rid of old practices that drive unhappiness in the workplace, doing away with near-illegal work hours, lack of trust and transparency, and improper human treatment. This book gives some recommendations as to how you can do so, which in turn creates \"work happiness\" for yourself and those around you.",
            "highlights": [
              "leader"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Using breath-taking art and enjoyabke storytelling, I take readers on a journey through some of my learnings on how, as leaders, we can chill the f*** out about productivity and profit—and start treating those around us like the living, breathing humans they are.",
            "highlights": [
              "breath-taking"
            ],
            "strong": [
              "Using breath-taking art and enjoyabke storytelling, I take readers on a journey through some of my learnings on how, as leaders, we can chill the f*** out about productivity and profit—and start treating those around us like the living, breathing humans they are."
            ]
          }
        ],
        "highlight": "really"
      },
